{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\n\nThe code-review documentation specialist declares `execution_mode: single_turn`, while its routing entry declares `exec: 1-TURN`. The runner therefore withholds repository tools. Its rubric also requires every contradiction to appear entirely inside the diff. This prevents grounded detection when a changed public contract requires an update to maintained documentation. The rubric does not apply the documentation roles and correction rules in `docs/documentation-policy.md`.\n\nThe approved design upgrades this specialist to the same agentic execution model used by other repository-grounded code-review criteria. It preserves advisory treatment and rejects stylistic enforcement.\n\n## Plan\n\n- Change `src/rebar/llm/reviewers/code-review-docs.md` to declare `execution_mode: agentic`. Change the `docs` entry in `src/rebar/llm/code_review/criteria_routing.json` to declare `exec: AGENT`.\n- Regenerate `src/rebar/llm/reviewers/index.json` from prompt front matter.\n- Revise the documentation rubric to require read-only repository navigation before reporting missing updates or role violations.\n- Replace the diff-only contradiction rule with a two-source rule. Every finding must cite a changed `path:line` plus a second repository source that proves inaccuracy, required ownership, or a bounded omission.\n- Add a missing-update check for changed user, operator, API, CLI, configuration, or shipped-help contracts. Permit absence findings only when repository evidence establishes the canonical documentation location and a bounded search confirms the omission. A repository-wide search with no match is insufficient.\n- Add a documentation-role check based on `docs/documentation-policy.md` and `docs/generated-artifacts.md`. Apply it to changed maintained documentation, shipped help, comments, ADRs, or generated artifacts. Require policy citations. Require abstention when audience, role, or ownership is ambiguous.\n- Update `tests/unit/test_code_review_nit_suppression.py`. Remove its obsolete `test_docs_rubric_forbids_absence_speculation` and `test_docs_rubric_requires_both_sides_in_diff` assertions because they pin the diff-only rule being replaced. Preserve its nit-suppression behavior coverage.\n- Add `tests/unit/test_code_review_docs_overlay.py` to pin agentic execution, repository-backed evidence, bounded omission checks, documentation roles, exclusions, and unchanged routing posture.\n- Add `src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/code-review-docs.eval.yaml` with balanced fire and no-fire cases. Add that specification to the standing offline validation set in `tests/unit/test_code_review_evals.py`.\n- Preserve the existing automatic file globs, advisory posture, blocking setting, impact-aware nit suppression, and independent Pass 2 verification. Do not add punctuation, character, vocabulary, diction, tone, wrapping, or subjective concision enforcement.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The documentation prompt declares agentic execution.\n- [ ] The documentation routing entry declares AGENT execution.\n- [ ] The generated reviewer index matches the updated prompt front matter.\n- [ ] The rubric directs the specialist to use read-only repository navigation.\n- [ ] Every finding requires a changed-text anchor.\n- [ ] Every finding requires a second repository citation.\n- [ ] A missing-update finding requires a repository-proven documentation obligation.\n- [ ] A missing-update finding requires a bounded search of the owned location.\n- [ ] A repository-wide search with no match cannot establish a missing-update finding.\n- [ ] Documentation-role findings cite an explicit role or correction rule from `docs/documentation-policy.md`.\n- [ ] Generated-output findings cite ownership from `docs/generated-artifacts.md`.\n- [ ] Ambiguous audience, ownership, or role produces no finding.\n- [ ] Protected evidence, quotations, historical ticket events, or ADR decision substance remain outside the criterion.\n- [ ] Punctuation, characters, vocabulary, diction, tone, wrapping, or subjective concision remain outside the criterion.\n- [ ] Automatic documentation routing globs remain unchanged.\n- [ ] The documentation criterion remains advisory.\n- [ ] The documentation criterion remains nonblocking.\n- [ ] Impact-aware nit suppression remains enabled.\n- [ ] Independent Pass 2 verification remains unchanged.\n- [ ] Prompt regression coverage contains proven omission and role-violation cases.\n- [ ] Prompt regression coverage contains internal-only, ambiguous-ownership, protected-evidence, or unrelated-documentation no-fire cases.\n- [ ] Focused prompt, routing, index, eval, lint, and type-check commands pass."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787680308853283001,"uuid":"5fe28cf3-794c-4e8e-bcab-92b325942b39"}